WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.079 --> 00:00:05.500
Hey youtubers it's Charlie this week for my
bonus Arrow video I wanted to talk about my

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:09.400
top 10 characters from season 2. I'm excluding
Oliver and most of Team Arrow, just because

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:13.070
they would hog half the list and there were
a bunch of new characters that deserve to

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:17.539
be mentioned. I'm still catching up after
being out of town, so instead of doing separate

00:00:17.539 --> 00:00:21.650
Flash video this week I'm just going to do
a quick update on some new info.

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:25.660
If you're finding me for the first time I
do Marvel and DC videos every week. Be sure

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:29.769
to subscribe to get everything. Feel free
to leave me suggestions for bonus topics about

00:00:29.769 --> 00:00:30.240
any of the comic book tv shows or movies.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:36.229
So before we do Arrow, the big Flash update
is that the producers confirmed John Wesley

00:00:36.229 --> 00:00:41.620
Shipp was playing Barry Allen's father, Henry
Allen. He's going to be in several episodes.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:45.979
In the comics his character dies in prison,
so either the show will just use him in a

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:51.309
lot of flashbacks or they'll change the comic
story so he can be alive in present day. Either

00:00:51.309 --> 00:00:52.750
way it's confirmed.

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:58.570
Now, let's talk about the best Arrow characters,
starting with number 10 - Doctor Ivo

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:02.379
Such a huge villain from the comics, I got
really excited when I heard he was going to

00:01:02.379 --> 00:01:06.630
be on the show. They opted to dial him way
back from his comic book persona and make

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:11.130
him more of a tragic villain at the end of
his rope. They did humanize him eventually

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:16.630
teasing his daughter and wife. But the biggest
easter egg was the Amazo Boat. Amazo for those

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:23.630
who don't know is a Justice League villain,
he's like DCs version of Ultron with a few

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:28.550
differences. Amazo can mimic anyone's powers.
So think of the future Sentinels from Days

00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:32.130
of Future Past.

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:36.970
I was a little disappointed they didn't tease
the Amazo Android, but because Season 2 was

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:41.250
all about the mirakuru serum I understand
why they kept a lot of comic book stuff out.

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:45.740
Everyone also started wondering if he was
secretly Felicity's father. I think, given

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:49.960
what the producers have said and the way things
went down, that's not the case and Felicity's

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:52.150
dad will turn out to be someone even cooler.

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:58.690
Ivo on the other hand could totally have been
doing other types of research we just didn't

00:01:58.690 --> 00:02:03.900
see. The way I think about comic book stuff
is like this. If you don't see it on the show

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:08.310
and none of the actors or producers ever talk
about it. There's still a chance it could

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:14.910
happen in a future season. So we could totally
see an android down the line. Until someone

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:21.910
says definitely not, it's still floating around
in an imaginary closet.

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:23.280
9 - Brother Blood

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:28.670
Kevin Alejandro really came into his own in
the second half of the season, they turned

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:32.800
the demonic aspects of the character from
the comics into metaphorical ones. Brother

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:39.800
Blood talked about wearing the mask as a way
to conquer his demons. On the show he ended

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:46.490
up becoming more of an analog for The Scarecrow
from The Dark Knight Trilogy. A scientist

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:49.620
with a formula.
Before we learned all the details about the

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:53.870
mirakuru I actually thought the League of
Assassin's was helping him just because of

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:56.430
the fear toxin in Batman Begins.

00:02:56.430 --> 00:03:01.099
A lot of you guys asked me if he maybe secretly
survived being stabbed by Isabel and all I

00:03:01.099 --> 00:03:07.480
can say is until the producers confirm he's
dead or we see a severed head. He can always

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:10.120
come back. Think of it as comic book logic.

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:12.180
8 - Malcolm Merlyn

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:17.220
I think the real crime on Arrow this year
was that John Barrowman didn't get more episodes.

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:21.610
And based on what's going on in Season 3 it
sounds like the writers agree. John Barrowman

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:26.239
was upgraded to cast regular for Season 3
meaning he's going to be in most of the episodes.

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:29.069
Like more than half of them which is 12 or
13.

00:03:29.069 --> 00:03:34.739
Even though he only appeared a few times,
he's one of the most memorable actors playing

00:03:34.739 --> 00:03:39.310
one of the biggest Green Arrow comic book
villains. He's essentially meant to be a foil

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:42.920
to Oliver. Like the darkest timeline version
of Oliver.

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:47.690
So when we start talking more about Oliver's
Journey in Season 3, we'll be able to figure

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:49.489
out some of what Merlyn is doing.

00:03:49.489 --> 00:03:54.010
So far my biggest prediction is that Oliver
will be in rebuilding mode all season and

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:56.800
going back to basics. The focus on the first
couple of episodes will be the core team arrow.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:01.900
Stephen Amell said Oliver and Laurel really
haven't addressed the big WTF secret identity

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:05.780
in the room yet. So that makes me think she's
not going to formally become a member of Team

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:08.160
Arrow till later in the season.

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:13.459
That means Merlyn is probably in rebuilding
mode too and Thea is just the first member

00:04:13.459 --> 00:04:18.729
of his new team. Thematically I always like
it better when each character has an opposite.

00:04:18.729 --> 00:04:23.669
Like Oliver and Malcolm. I think we can call
Thea Roy's new opposite. I'm sure he'll be

00:04:23.669 --> 00:04:25.830
really happy to learn about that.

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:27.009
7 - Sin

00:04:27.009 --> 00:04:31.900
How can you not love Roy and Sin during the
second half of the season. I was bummed she

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:35.900
didn't get more episodes too, and that she
was kept out of the loop on everything. She

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:40.120
didn't know anything about the mirakuru, Sara
never told her about the League of Assassins

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:44.610
and they never really addressed what her character
would be doing now that she was on her own

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:45.020
again.

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:48.110
It was only implied, but I think we'll see
more of her helping Roy with missions. I'd

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:50.210
really like to see her become a formal member
of Team Arrow by the end of Season 3. Plus

00:04:50.210 --> 00:04:53.580
there's always the possibility of the Young
Justice spinoff. She could totally become

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:58.249
a part of that if it ever happens.
My favorite Sin moment was her and Roy trying

00:04:58.249 --> 00:05:00.839
to fight crime on their own.

00:05:00.839 --> 00:05:03.460
6 - Roy

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:07.559
My opinion on his character did a major 180
from the beginning of the season to the end.

00:05:07.559 --> 00:05:12.599
That's just the magic of a character arc.
Laurel was on one too. But I like Roy's more.

00:05:12.599 --> 00:05:16.629
Almost homeless dude gets injected with super
serum, goes crazy, survives and becomes member

00:05:16.629 --> 00:05:20.909
of a mini Justice League. If only it were
that simple in real life.

00:05:20.909 --> 00:05:24.919
My favorite Roy moments were training with
Oliver and when he was first trying to figure

00:05:24.919 --> 00:05:30.699
out his powers after episode 10.

00:05:30.699 --> 00:05:36.509
5 - Nyssa Al Ghul

00:05:36.509 --> 00:05:40.180
One of the best new female characters on the
show. She was a master assassin that could

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:45.189
match Oliver in a fight, had the might of
Ra's Al Ghul at her back and in an interesting

00:05:45.189 --> 00:05:49.110
twist, was one of the only LGBT characters
this season.

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:52.539
She was so awesome, there is no way the show
is not bringing her back.

00:05:52.539 --> 00:05:57.710
My favorite Nyssa moment was actually a funny
one, it was at the end of the season when

00:05:57.710 --> 00:06:00.119
she met Felicity and they had a little stand-off
moment. It almost looked like she was looking

00:06:00.119 --> 00:06:04.680
at Felicity as sex object like she was sexually
attracted to her.

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:09.610
Tumblr, I'm going to task you with making
that reaction gif.

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:12.009
4 - The Canary

00:06:12.009 --> 00:06:17.309
Caity Lotz had the hard task of stepping in
between Laurel and Oliver as a romantic foil,

00:06:17.309 --> 00:06:22.249
but I got so excited when I saw her for the
first time. I took the first half of the season

00:06:22.249 --> 00:06:26.349
to figure out where her character was headed
and yes I do wish she could have spent more

00:06:26.349 --> 00:06:33.279
time teaming up with Oliver on missions. She
also had this really funny relationship with

00:06:33.279 --> 00:06:36.969
Felicity that went from distrust to mutual
respect.

00:06:36.969 --> 00:06:42.610
There was a brief moment when I thought she
we going to out Felicity Felicity, but spoiler

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:47.149
alert, that's impossible. There is only one
quirky tech genius on Team Arrow and she went

00:06:47.149 --> 00:06:48.199
to MIT.

00:06:48.199 --> 00:06:54.629
Sara can always come back for League of Assassins
or Laurel tie-ins, but for the most part I

00:06:54.629 --> 00:06:58.929
think Caity Lotz is off the show. I'm really
happy that they left her character's exit

00:06:58.929 --> 00:07:01.899
very open-ended. As in, she didn't die.

00:07:01.899 --> 00:07:05.460
Passing that black canary jacket on to Laurel
is heavy foreshadowing.

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:07.699
3 - Amanda Waller

00:07:07.699 --> 00:07:12.249
Hands down biggest new non-villain badass
on the show. I say non-villain, but she's

00:07:12.249 --> 00:07:17.069
really a neutral figure in the DC Universe.
She serves the government ultimately, so sometimes

00:07:17.069 --> 00:07:22.819
that takes her against superheroes. She tied
up a few big plot threads from season 1 and

00:07:22.819 --> 00:07:28.059
started a few brand new ones in season 2 that
will largely inform the Hong Kong flashbacks

00:07:28.059 --> 00:07:29.409
in Season 3.

00:07:29.409 --> 00:07:33.499
She's like one of those Halo characters the
show will probably never kill just because

00:07:33.499 --> 00:07:38.409
they're too interesting. Stephen Amell also
confirmed one of our biggest theories. Amanda

00:07:38.409 --> 00:07:44.610
Waller was that woman with the Red Shoes behind
the whole Edward Fyers China plot. They were

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:48.809
trying to decimate China's economy.

00:07:48.809 --> 00:07:52.949
One of the biggest things I'm looking forward
to in Season 3 is the Hong Kong flashbacks

00:07:52.949 --> 00:07:56.619
telingl the story of Oliver and Waller's relationship.

00:07:56.619 --> 00:07:58.969
2 - Barry Allen

00:07:58.969 --> 00:08:05.199
Never has a new character so naturally become
a member of Team Arrow. Just talking about

00:08:05.199 --> 00:08:09.059
the character first, Barry was the perfect
call to action for Oliver in the first half

00:08:09.059 --> 00:08:13.369
of the Season. He's the one that gave him
that Green Arrow mask. Like he helped Oliver

00:08:13.369 --> 00:08:16.619
make a giant leap forward in his hero's journey.

00:08:16.619 --> 00:08:22.849
Obviously there's all the spinoff stuff going
on too. Based on the pilot episode, the CW

00:08:22.849 --> 00:08:26.899
is saying that The Flash will be one of the
best new shows they've had in the last 10

00:08:26.899 --> 00:08:32.320
years. There's a lot of reasons for that,
but having a very fun and positive lead character

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:37.979
like Barry Allen makes it a lot easier to
make a show people can get excited about.

00:08:37.979 --> 00:08:43.910
Grant Gustin did an amazing job, before his
cameo on Arrow I only knew him from Glee.

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:49.590
And on that show he was something of a villain.
I don't see a lot of villain inside Barry

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:56.300
Allen, but I'm interested to see how he adds
some complexity to the character.

00:08:56.300 --> 00:09:01.580
I think of him as being tortured, but if we're
comparing grumpy superheroes. Oliver would

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:08.580
win hands down. Barry is this hyper active
superhero fanboy. And look at how brightly

00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:15.840
lit all of the scenes in the trailer are.
This isn't going to be noir like Arrow or

00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:22.800
Gotham.

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:24.200
1 - Deathstroke

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:28.950
Manu Bennett is an amazing actor and he had
two full years to develop his Slade Wilson

00:09:28.950 --> 00:09:33.590
character. The Deathstroke persona didn't
really develop until season 2. And even then,

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:36.500
it really didn't manifest until halfway through
the season.

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:40.750
He's going to go down in Arrow history as
one of the all time best villains, which creates

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:42.700
some issues for season 3. How do you top Slade?
He was like Macbeth on steroids.

00:09:42.700 --> 00:09:47.400
I'm really hoping that the show uses him as
like a Hannibal Lecter character next season.

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:51.360
Like Oliver goes to him for help with whoever
ends up being the new villain. I actually

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:58.360
asked you guys to submit your fan art of Slade
as Hannibal so High Fives to Sumit Shetty.

00:09:59.280 --> 00:09:59.960
Very cool.

00:09:59.960 --> 00:10:04.570
I'll probably do more fanart submission videos
for other stuff in the future for anyone who's

00:10:04.570 --> 00:10:04.890
interested.

00:10:04.890 --> 00:10:10.510
So I realize I had to leave ton of awesome
characters off this list, but let me know

00:10:10.510 --> 00:10:14.760
who your favorite was in Season 2 and what
your favorite scene of theirs was.

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:19.080
I'm still catching up after being out of town
for 4 days, but tomorrow I'm doing my regular

00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:24.160
Arrow/Flash Q&amp;A and a Maleficent Review if
I can see it early enough. Be sure to subscribe

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:30.880
to get everything. Otherwise that second thursday
video will be Marvel or Star Wars that I missed

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:35.110
yesterday. I'm definitely doing a Maleficent
Review before Saturday though.

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:40.860
Right now click here to learn more about Arrow
Season 3 and the Flash and click here for

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:42.430
my X-Men Days of Future Past Review.

00:10:42.430 --> 00:10:44.350
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow.
High Fives!

